{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39836956",
      "title": "Handling HTTP Errors",
      "sourceHash": "986a29d3565dcda07497515fcb787d23ceef174056d42cf33b85cd4e6004b5e7",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.54,
          "end": 2.22,
          "en": "So we're making good progress,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.22,
          "end": 5.58,
          "en": "and we're fetching data and using that fetched data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.58,
          "end": 8.85,
          "en": "and we're also managing that loading state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.85,
          "end": 12.21,
          "en": "Now, another situation you may frequently face",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.21,
          "end": 16.56,
          "en": "when sending HTTP requests are errors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.56,
          "end": 19.5,
          "en": "because when sending HTTP requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.5,
          "end": 24.15,
          "en": "there are many reasons for why things may fail,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.15,
          "end": 27.78,
          "en": "because a user lost their network connection,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.78,
          "end": 30.99,
          "en": "because maybe something went wrong on the back end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.99,
          "end": 34.83,
          "en": "the server might be temporarily offline, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.83,
          "end": 38.13,
          "en": "or you have some bug in your code there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.13,
          "end": 42.09,
          "en": "Whatever the reason may be, errors can occur,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.09,
          "end": 45,
          "en": "and therefore, in your front-end code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45,
          "end": 48.09,
          "en": "you should also be prepared for the scenario",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.09,
          "end": 51.09,
          "en": "that fetching the data might fail,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.09,
          "end": 52.83,
          "en": "and there are two main ways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.83,
          "end": 56.22,
          "en": "of how fetching that data may fail.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.22,
          "end": 57.053,
          "en": "For one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.053,
          "end": 60.54,
          "en": "you might fail to send that request in the first place,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.54,
          "end": 64.77,
          "en": "for example, because the network connection crashed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.77,
          "end": 66.33,
          "en": "The other situation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.33,
          "end": 69.87,
          "en": "where sending the request may kind of fail",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.87,
          "end": 73.41,
          "en": "is that it is actually sent successfully to the back end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.41,
          "end": 75.75,
          "en": "but something goes wrong there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.75,
          "end": 79.32300000000001,
          "en": "and the back end sends back an error response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.19,
          "end": 82.863,
          "en": "and you typically wanna handle both cases.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.76,
          "end": 86.463,
          "en": "Now, let's start with the error response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.36,
          "end": 91.5,
          "en": "When using the fetch function for sending HTTP requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.5,
          "end": 96.36,
          "en": "you can check if the response is an error response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 96.36,
          "end": 99.693,
          "en": "by checking the response.ok property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 100.86,
          "end": 102.45,
          "en": "If this is true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.45,
          "end": 105.72,
          "en": "it means that you got a success response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.72,
          "end": 110.25,
          "en": "with a 200 or 300-ish status code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 110.25,
          "end": 114.47999999999999,
          "en": "If this is not true, so if it is false,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 114.47999999999999,
          "end": 117.93299999999999,
          "en": "you got a 400 or 500-ish status code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 119.13,
          "end": 124.13,
          "en": "so here, you wanna check if response is not ok,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 124.35,
          "end": 129.35,
          "en": "and if it is not ok, you wanna handle this situation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 130.65,
          "end": 133.62,
          "en": "For example, by throwing an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 133.62,
          "end": 136.62,
          "en": "Here, we could prepare an error object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 136.62,
          "end": 140.07999999999998,
          "en": "by instantiating the built-in Error class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 141.32999999999998,
          "end": 143.52,
          "en": "and set an error message that could be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 143.52,
          "end": 147.633,
          "en": "'Failed to fetch places' or something like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 148.92000000000002,
          "end": 151.173,
          "en": "and then we could throw that error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 152.31,
          "end": 154.953,
          "en": "or do that all in one step, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 156,
          "end": 157.95,
          "en": "Now, when you throw an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 157.95,
          "end": 160.14,
          "en": "you will crash the application, though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 160.14,
          "end": 162.78300000000002,
          "en": "which might not really be what you wanna do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 163.68,
          "end": 165.72,
          "en": "Therefore, you should wrap code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 165.72,
          "end": 169.41,
          "en": "that could potentially throw an error with try-catch,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 169.41,
          "end": 172.263,
          "en": "which you can do when using async/await.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 173.19,
          "end": 177.54,
          "en": "You can wrap try around the code that might fail.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 177.54,
          "end": 180.543,
          "en": "In this case, that's this code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 182.22,
          "end": 184.71,
          "en": "and then you can catch any errors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 184.71,
          "end": 186.15,
          "en": "that might have been thrown",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 186.15,
          "end": 188.88,
          "en": "and define code that should be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 188.88,
          "end": 191.133,
          "en": "if an error was encountered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 192.27,
          "end": 196.77,
          "en": "and this allows you to stop the application from crashing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 196.77,
          "end": 198.42000000000002,
          "en": "and enables you to define",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 198.42000000000002,
          "end": 201.32999999999998,
          "en": "which code should be executed instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 201.32999999999998,
          "end": 202.163,
          "en": "Now, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 202.163,
          "end": 205.35,
          "en": "here, I could have simply avoided throwing an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 205.35,
          "end": 208.38,
          "en": "and we would then not have needed try-catch,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 208.38,
          "end": 212.85,
          "en": "but the fetch function itself can actually also fail",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 212.85,
          "end": 214.41,
          "en": "and throw an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 214.41,
          "end": 217.86,
          "en": "For example, if there is no network connection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 217.86,
          "end": 221.1,
          "en": "That's why I definitely wanna use try-catch here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 221.1,
          "end": 222.24,
          "en": "and throw an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 222.24,
          "end": 225.96,
          "en": "if I decide that I'm not happy with the response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 225.96,
          "end": 228.99,
          "en": "so that either way we end up in this catch block",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 228.99,
          "end": 230.793,
          "en": "if anything goes wrong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 232.32,
          "end": 233.91,
          "en": "Well, and here in the catch block,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 233.91,
          "end": 236.28,
          "en": "we can now handle the error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 236.28,
          "end": 240.72,
          "en": "and, of course, handling the error in a React application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 240.72,
          "end": 244.02,
          "en": "typically means that we wanna update the UI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 244.02,
          "end": 247.2,
          "en": "and show an error message to the user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 247.2,
          "end": 248.73,
          "en": "and that, of course, means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 248.73,
          "end": 253.32,
          "en": "that we need a third piece of state, an error state here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 253.32,
          "end": 254.67,
          "en": "so I'll name it error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 254.67,
          "end": 257.703,
          "en": "and have a state updating function that's called setError,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 259.62,
          "end": 263.4,
          "en": "and when fetching data, it's super-common",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 263.4,
          "end": 267.84,
          "en": "to have these three pieces of state work together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 267.84,
          "end": 269.25,
          "en": "The data state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 269.25,
          "end": 272.67,
          "en": "where you store the data that you're fetching,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 272.67,
          "end": 275.4,
          "en": "the loading state, which you use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 275.4,
          "end": 279.72,
          "en": "to tell the user that you are currently fetching data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 279.72,
          "end": 281.61,
          "en": "and the error state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 281.61,
          "end": 286.5,
          "en": "which you use to show potential errors on the screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 286.5,
          "end": 288.96,
          "en": "and now, with that error state added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 288.96,
          "end": 293.96,
          "en": "we can set the error here in our catch block,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 294.33,
          "end": 295.17,
          "en": "and, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 295.17,
          "end": 299.67,
          "en": "set this error object as a value for error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 299.67,
          "end": 303.57,
          "en": "This will be an error object that contains an error message,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 303.57,
          "end": 307.32,
          "en": "for example, this error message which we're setting here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 307.32,
          "end": 311.28,
          "en": "Now, before using this error state to update the UI,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 311.28,
          "end": 314.01,
          "en": "there also is one other thing we should do here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 314.01,
          "end": 315.99,
          "en": "when using try-catch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 315.99,
          "end": 320.31,
          "en": "because you might already see those red squiggly lines here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 320.31,
          "end": 321.54,
          "en": "We're getting those",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 321.54,
          "end": 325.56,
          "en": "because here I'm trying to update my available places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 325.56,
          "end": 329.37,
          "en": "based on data that's inside of that try block.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 329.37,
          "end": 333.33,
          "en": "Now, if we do face an error, in this step here, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 333.33,
          "end": 336.51,
          "en": "we will never have response data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 336.51,
          "end": 339.033,
          "en": "so trying to set it here won't work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 339.9,
          "end": 343.95,
          "en": "Instead, we should move this code into this try block",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 343.95,
          "end": 344.783,
          "en": "because here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 344.783,
          "end": 348.21,
          "en": "we know that when we make it to the end of this block,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 348.21,
          "end": 349.743,
          "en": "all the data will be there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 351.69,
          "end": 354.06,
          "en": "On the other hand, setIsFetching false",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 354.06,
          "end": 357.93,
          "en": "should stay outside of the try-catch block, typically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 357.93,
          "end": 361.08,
          "en": "because I wanna end this loading state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 361.08,
          "end": 364.53,
          "en": "no matter if we got an error or not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 364.53,
          "end": 367.89,
          "en": "because even if we failed to fetch places data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 367.89,
          "end": 370.56,
          "en": "we're still not fetching it anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 370.56,
          "end": 372.42,
          "en": "We're not loading the data anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 372.42,
          "end": 375.9,
          "en": "We just got an error, but we're not fetching it anymore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 375.9,
          "end": 378.453,
          "en": "so this should be set to false either way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 380.19,
          "end": 382.56,
          "en": "but with that, we can now use this error state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 382.56,
          "end": 384.36,
          "en": "to update the UI,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 384.36,
          "end": 386.1,
          "en": "and for this, in this component here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 386.1,
          "end": 389.28,
          "en": "I'll simply check if error is truthy,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 389.28,
          "end": 392.82,
          "en": "so if we have an error, and if that's the case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 392.82,
          "end": 395.85,
          "en": "I wanna return a separate error component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 395.85,
          "end": 399.33299999999997,
          "en": "which I prepared in advance and which you find attached.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 400.32,
          "end": 402.78,
          "en": "You should add this Error.jsx file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 402.78,
          "end": 405.87,
          "en": "which you'll find attached in your components folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 405.87,
          "end": 408,
          "en": "and this is simply a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 408,
          "end": 410.4,
          "en": "that will output a title and a message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 410.4,
          "end": 413.493,
          "en": "and that will also later allow us to dismiss it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 415.8,
          "end": 417.65999999999997,
          "en": "Here, in AvailablePlaces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 417.65999999999997,
          "end": 419.94,
          "en": "I'm not interested in dismissing it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 419.94,
          "end": 424.443,
          "en": "Instead, I just want to render this Error component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 425.37,
          "end": 429.333,
          "en": "and for that, of course, you must import it from Error.jsx,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 431.61,
          "end": 434.94,
          "en": "and then, with it imported and rendered down there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 434.94,
          "end": 439.5,
          "en": "you must set a title, for example, \"An error occurred!\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 439.5,
          "end": 440.82,
          "en": "and then a message,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 440.82,
          "end": 444.39,
          "en": "and the message here is my error.message,",
